    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1237">

                <pb facs="0865" n="749" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg749"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.512/333.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Consul General Hanna.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-07-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 15, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your July 13. You say instructions have been sent to Gulf port authorities to
                    accept New York exchange in lieu of Mexican gold at current rate of exchange,
                    one for two.</p>
                <pb facs="0866" n="750" xml:id="pg750"/>
                <p>Department does not understand what you mean by one for two, as current rate of
                    exchange is more like one for three. Please explain.</p>
                <p>Will not General Carranza arrange that bar and other taxes may be paid in
                    Constitutionalist currency?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
